  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Luna measures three sides of a rectangle, and their lengths total to $27\\text{ cm}$. Mateo measures three sides of the same rectangle, and their lengths total to $33\\text{ cm}$. Find the perimeter of the rectangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$40\\text{ cm}$.\n\nAdding the two three-side totals gives three times the sum of adjacent sides.",
      "worked": "Let the adjacent side lengths be $a\\text{ cm}$ and $b\\text{ cm}$. The distinct three-side totals give $2a+b=27$ and $a+2b=33$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3a+3b&=27+33\\\\3(a+b)&=60\\\\a+b&=20\\\\P&=2(a+b)\\\\P&=40\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
